7565.1 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=54 visible=54 resolved=54 missing=0 materials=54 triangles=151121 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=HIMALAYAN/HIMALAYA_ROCK01_BLEND04 resource=materials/himalayan/himalaya_rock01_ssbump.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 54 visible materials that name one of 25 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
7565.1 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=refused declared=5 visible=5 resolved=5 missing=0 materials=5 triangles=86336 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=HIMALAYAN/HIMALAYA_ROCK01_BLEND04 resource=materials/Nature/snow_full001_normal.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 1/5 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
7565.1 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=28 visible=28 resolved=0 missing=28 materials=28 triangles=28335 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=FRANKENIZER/CRYPTWALL2A resource=materials/overlays/detail001.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 28 of 28 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; 1 material names a %detailtype group (first=tf_grass); %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
